All 28 tests pass, including `size_hint_overflow`.

The fix in `tokio-stream/src/stream_map.rs:686`:

```rust
fn size_hint(&self) -> (usize, Option<usize>) {
    let mut ret = (0usize, Some(0usize));

    for (_, stream) in &self.entries {
        let hint = stream.size_hint();

        ret.0 = ret.0.saturating_add(hint.0);

        match (ret.1, hint.1) {
            (Some(a), Some(b)) => ret.1 = a.checked_add(b),
            (Some(_), None) => ret.1 = None,
            _ => {}
        }
    }

    ret
}
```

- Lower bound uses `saturating_add`, so it clamps to `usize::MAX` rather than panicking (debug) or wrapping to a bogus small value (release).
- Upper bound uses `checked_add`, collapsing to `None` on overflow — the correct signal for "no representable upper bound", and consistent with how an unbounded child stream is already handled.

The `0usize`/`Some(0usize)` annotations are needed because the accumulator would otherwise be an ambiguous `{integer}` at the point the methods are called.
